From 00f03a4c5e153b29d3f3e9a7acb938fffa81ef2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bryamzxz <bryamestebanvargas@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 15:53:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(esp_netif): restore DHCP_CLIENT whitelist in dhcpc_cb
 store path

esp_netif_internal_dhcpc_cb is invoked for any LWIP_NSC_IPV4_*_CHANGED
event, including a manual netif_set_addr() on a custom netif that never
started DHCP. Calling dhcp_ip_addr_store() on such a netif dereferences
netif_dhcp_data(netif), which is NULL unless dhcp_start() ran, and
panics from the lwIP task with LoadProhibited at dhcp_state.c:52.

The original 2018 implementation of dhcp_state.c gated all three
state-store entry points on a VALID_NETIF_ID(netif) macro that checked
ESP_NETIF_DHCP_CLIENT. That whitelist was removed silently during the
refactor in 356bc603c4 ("lwip: Support DHCP restore last IP",
2022-03-23) when the function signatures changed from void* to
struct netif* and direct esp_netif access was dropped.

The bug surfaced for PPPoS in 2024 (esp-protocols#800) and was
band-aided in c8c10214f8 ("fix(esp_netif): Fix incorrect DHCP call for
PPP interfaces", 2025-04-14) by adding a !_IS_NETIF_ANY_POINT2POINT_TYPE
gate at the call site. That fix only covers PPP; non-PPP custom netifs
that carry static IP without DHCP (e.g. raw-IP overlay carriers such as
WireGuard tunnel netifs) still hit the same crash.

Replace the PPP blacklist with the original DHCP_CLIENT whitelist. PPP
netifs are still skipped because they do not have ESP_NETIF_DHCP_CLIENT
set, so the regression closed by c8c10214f8 stays closed. Any future
non-DHCP netif type is now also covered without needing per-type gates.

Reproducer: create an esp_netif via esp_netif_new() without setting
ESP_NETIF_FLAG_IS_PPP and without enabling ESP_NETIF_DHCP_CLIENT,
attach a static IP, then call netif_set_addr() on the underlying lwIP
netif. With CONFIG_LWIP_DHCP_RESTORE_LAST_IP=y the firmware crashes
from the lwIP task with the same backtrace shape reported in
esp-protocols#800.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 components/esp_netif/lwip/esp_netif_lwip.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/esp_netif/lwip/esp_netif_lwip.c b/components/esp_netif/lwip/esp_netif_lwip.c
index dcdbc53082..26f5dd9401 100644
--- a/components/esp_netif/lwip/esp_netif_lwip.c
+++ b/components/esp_netif/lwip/esp_netif_lwip.c
@@ -1456,11 +1456,21 @@ static void esp_netif_internal_dhcpc_cb(struct netif *netif)
             }
 #ifdef CONFIG_LWIP_DHCP_RESTORE_LAST_IP
             /*
-             * Store the IP address only for non-Point-to-Point interfaces.
-             * P2P interfaces (like PPP) have dynamic addressing that shouldn't be stored
-             * for later restoration, as they're negotiated on each connection.
+             * Store the IP address only for interfaces that actually run the
+             * DHCP client. dhcp_ip_addr_store() reads netif_dhcp_data(netif)
+             * which is NULL unless dhcp_start() ran for this netif, so calling
+             * it on any non-DHCP netif (PPP, raw-IP overlay carriers, etc.)
+             * dereferences NULL and panics from the lwIP task.
+             *
+             * This whitelist restores the invariant that existed in the
+             * original 2018 implementation of dhcp_state.c (macro
+             * VALID_NETIF_ID checking ESP_NETIF_DHCP_CLIENT) and was removed
+             * during the refactor in 356bc603c4. The PPP-specific gate added
+             * in c8c10214f8 (closes esp-protocols#800) was a partial
+             * restoration; this is the symmetric whitelist that covers all
+             * non-DHCP netif types.
              */
-            if (!_IS_NETIF_ANY_POINT2POINT_TYPE(esp_netif)) {
+            if (esp_netif->flags & ESP_NETIF_DHCP_CLIENT) {
                 dhcp_ip_addr_store(netif);
             }
 #endif /* CONFIG_LWIP_DHCP_RESTORE_LAST_IP */
